\ ***************************************************************************
\ FREESCAPE for the BBC Master - where the logic calls what it leaves out
\ (tools/logic/hooks.py, by the original's addresses)
\
\ The logic calls these where the original calls its own routines. Each
\ does nothing yet (or answers that nothing was drawn or hit), as the
\ transcription's defaults do, which tools/logiccheck.mjs checks the logic
\ against. The renderer, the sound and the screen fill them in. They're in
\ main RAM, called from either of the logic's banks: one that pages
\ another bank in puts the caller's back before it returns (logic_paged
\ says which: LDA logic_paged : STA romsel). They may use any of the pool's bytes
\ the logic isn't using across the call (baron's allocator sees to it).
\
\ An includer that fills one in names its own routine before including
\ this file, as LOGIC_HOOK_SOUND, LOGIC_HOOK_WAIT, LOGIC_HOOK_WALKED,
\ LOGIC_HOOK_LOADED or LOGIC_HOOK_REDRAW (src/live.6502 does), and the hook
\ is that routine.
\ ***************************************************************************

\ hook_sound ($9574): play sound A (the original waits while it plays).
IF DEFINED(LOGIC_HOOK_SOUND)
    hook_sound = LOGIC_HOOK_SOUND
ELSE
.hook_sound
    RTS
ENDIF

\ hook_wait: wait while the interrupt counts Countdown down from A frames
\ (the turn's and step's size keys, 7; the crosshair keys, 9; FCL DELAY).
\ Countdown is 0 once the logic goes on.
IF DEFINED(LOGIC_HOOK_WAIT)
    hook_wait = LOGIC_HOOK_WAIT
ELSE
.hook_wait
    RTS
ENDIF

\ hook_walked (the move, $A220, once the walk is done and before the
\ margin): TargetX, TargetY and TargetZ are where the walk stopped, and
\ PlayerX, PlayerY and PlayerZ where it began (on the probe's step, the
\ feet), so the segment between is what the move checked. Not the
\ original's: it's for the frames shown between passes (decision 4).
IF DEFINED(LOGIC_HOOK_WALKED)
    hook_walked = LOGIC_HOOK_WALKED
ELSE
.hook_walked
    RTS
ENDIF

\ hook_loaded (an area's load, $BE18, as it begins): the camera is about to
\ be put somewhere new, maybe in another area, rather than moved. Not the
\ original's: it's for the frames shown between passes.
IF DEFINED(LOGIC_HOOK_LOADED)
    hook_loaded = LOGIC_HOOK_LOADED
ELSE
.hook_loaded
    RTS
ENDIF

\ hook_key_lights ($99AE, $9A64): the panel's key lights, A = 0 off, 1 on.
.hook_key_lights
    RTS

\ hook_panel ($B72B): redraw the panel's figures that GameFlags and
\ GameFlags2 say changed (SPACE calls it with GameFlags 1).
.hook_panel
    RTS

\ hook_crosshair ($AAA0): draw or erase (by EOR) the crosshair at CrossX,
\ CrossY.
.hook_crosshair
    RTS

\ hook_screen_colours ($A77A after its first lines): the view takes
\ ScreenColours.
.hook_screen_colours
    RTS

\ hook_redraw (FCL REDRAW): the redraw, the copy (which plays Sound and
\ clears it), the sensors' tests and the panel, there and then.
IF DEFINED(LOGIC_HOOK_REDRAW)
    hook_redraw = LOGIC_HOOK_REDRAW
ELSE
.hook_redraw
    RTS
ENDIF

\ hook_undraw ($B492): hiding object A, which the last redraw's draw list
\ may hold (NDrawn is its length); C set if it did, which asks for a redraw
\ from the list (GameFlags2 bit 3).
.hook_undraw
    CLC
    RTS

\ hook_sensor_off ($B467): sensor A is hidden: it stops firing.
.hook_sensor_off
    RTS

\ hook_laser ($AA50-$AA8C): the laser's lines from the view's corners (EOR:
\ called twice, to draw and to erase).
IF DEFINED(LOGIC_HOOK_LASER)
    hook_laser = LOGIC_HOOK_LASER
ELSE
.hook_laser
    RTS
ENDIF

\ hook_shot ($B153): the object under the crosshair into Collided, from
\ the renderer's projected faces (unchanged if none is under it). Called
\ with LOGIC_CODE_BANK paged: the live disc's is there (src/laser.6502).
IF DEFINED(LOGIC_HOOK_SHOT)
    hook_shot = LOGIC_HOOK_SHOT
ELSE
.hook_shot
    RTS
ENDIF

\ hook_message ($93C4, $BCA6): the 14 characters at Y X (in LOGIC_BANK,
\ which is in, or main RAM) shown, highlighted, in the panel's message
\ line: the rigs' messages. The wait after it is hook_wait's.
IF DEFINED(LOGIC_HOOK_MESSAGE)
    hook_message = LOGIC_HOOK_MESSAGE
ELSE
.hook_message
    RTS
ENDIF

\ hook_info ($C3DC): I shows the information screen and waits for a key.
.hook_info
    RTS

\ hook_game_over ($9AB7): GameOver is set: the end of the game.
.hook_game_over
    RTS
